**Add `spy: true` option to mocks.**

According to coding guidelines, all `vi.mock()` calls should include the `spy: true` option for consistent mocking patterns.



As per coding guidelines for `**/*.test.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}`.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-vi.mock('node:fs/promises');
-vi.mock('glob');
-vi.mock('storybook/internal/node-logger');
-vi.mock('./component-analyzer');
+vi.mock('node:fs/promises', { spy: true });
+vi.mock('glob', { spy: true });
+vi.mock('storybook/internal/node-logger', { spy: true });
+vi.mock('./component-analyzer', { spy: true });
```
</details>

